@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Environments with their own resolve.conditions resolve a dependency through exactly those conditions in dev, with the dependency inlined and externalized (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 The same environments resolve the same entries in build (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-2]
+- [ ] 1.3 The ssr environment with default conditions resolves the default entry and the worker environment the worker entry (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/environment.spec.ts) [AC-3]
+
+## 2. Conditions
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add DEV_PROD_CONDITION and the default client, ssr and external condition lists (packages/vite/src/node/constants.ts)
+- [ ] 2.2 Resolve exports and imports with the configured conditions only, replacing development|production by the mode, and drop overrideConditions (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/resolve.ts, packages/vite/src/node/packages.ts)
+- [ ] 2.3 Set the default conditions per consumer and keep ssr.target webworker working through keepProcessEnv and the build output defaults (packages/vite/src/node/config.ts, packages/vite/src/node/build.ts, packages/vite/src/node/plugins/define.ts)
+- [ ] 2.4 Resolve externalized SSR imports with externalConditions, and the bundled config file with the node condition (packages/vite/src/node/ssr/fetchModule.ts, packages/vite/src/node/config.ts)
+
+## 3. Docs
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Document the defaults and the migration (docs/config/shared-options.md, docs/config/ssr-options.md, docs/guide/migration.md)
